.TH DANBY-CHANGINGENVIRONMENT 1
.SH NAME
danby-changingenvironment \- logistic growth with varying carrying capacity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/changingenvironment
.SH MODEL
N' = rN(1-N/K(t));
K(t) = K0(1+s sin(wt)).
.PP
The capacity varies independently of the population.  Its amplitude is
restricted below one so K remains positive.  Slow forcing lets the population
track capacity; fast forcing produces lag and a reduced response.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the population bar.  The four tracks set growth, mean capacity, variation,
and forcing frequency.  Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/changingenvironment.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/changingenvironment.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR populationmodel (2),
.IR numerics (2)
